# D18. Every direct module this tree may depend on, one path per line. The gate
# diffs the module graph against this file, so taking a new dependency is a
# visible change here rather than a line in go.mod nobody reads.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# The parent proposal's table says why each one is not the standard library.
# The ones it commits to that have not arrived yet, and the phase that brings
# each: x/crypto, x/sync, klauspost/compress (9), BurntSushi/toml (5), a
# pure-Go BLAKE3 (6), x/image (9).

golang.org/x/sys

# Argon2id password hashing, XChaCha20-Poly1305 at rest and MD4 for the SMB NT
# hash, none of which the standard library provides. Arrived with Phase 3's
# auth subsystem.
golang.org/x/crypto

# NFC and NFD candidate spellings, so a name another program wrote in either
# form is found as it is written. Arrived with Phase 1's path layer.
golang.org/x/text

# SQLite, translated to Go rather than wrapped, which is what keeps
# CGO_ENABLED=0 and with it the static binary and the toolchain-free cross
# build. Arrived with Phase 2's store.
modernc.org/sqlite

# The directory ETag hash, which is wire-visible so parity keeps it BLAKE3.
# Pure Go, so CGO_ENABLED=0 has no fallback to disable. Arrived with Phase 4's
# aggregate; Phase 6 reuses it for the client-selected upload checksum, which
# is why it is one entry here and one direct dependency rather than two.
lukechampine.com/blake3

# sc.toml, the one config file the product reads. It enters the module graph
# with Phase 5, which is the phase that parses it.
github.com/BurntSushi/toml

# BMP, TIFF and WebP decoding for the preview worker. The standard library
# covers JPEG, PNG and GIF; these three are what x/image adds, and all of them
# are pure Go, which is what keeps the decoders out of a C library and
# CGO_ENABLED=0 with nothing to fall back to. Arrived with Phase 9.
golang.org/x/image

# zstd for the search index's block compression. Pure Go, so CGO_ENABLED=0 has
# nothing to fall back to, and the format is what the two implementations agree
# on rather than the encoder's exact output. It enters the graph with Phase 8;
# the parent proposal's table lists it against Phase 9, which is the phase that
# was expected to need it first.
github.com/klauspost/compress

# The change channel for /api/events. The dependency decision was reopened
# because the protocol carries client frames (sub/unsub), so a hand-rolled
# frame layer would re-implement control-frame handling, close codes and
# fragmentation that a maintained module already owns.
github.com/gorilla/websocket
